  "body": "This has been discussed in the context of the Popup API within OpenUI, [here](https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/322#issuecomment-855145392). The general consensus there was to adopt a more \"parallel\" set of names for Popup, `show` and `hide`. The `<dialog>` API was called out for not being consistent: `show` and `close`. \r\n\r\nPerhaps we should consider deprecating `<dialog>.close()` and replacing it with `.hide()`? Unfortunately, Chromium doesn't have a use counter for `<dialog>.close()` but I would imagine it's close to the usage of [`.showModal()`](https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/3726) plus [`.show()`](https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/3725), which is around 0.025%. That's a surprisingly small percentage of the overall usage of the [dialog element](https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/481), which is around 4%. Perhaps most people are adding/removing the `open` attribute?\r\n",
